e>Hruska</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynisdottir</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arner</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanisms behind gender differences in circulating leptin levels</article-title><source>J. Int. Med.</source><volume>247</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>462</lpage><year>2000</year></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miravitlles</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fernandez</surname><given-names>I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Guerrero</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Murio</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Development and results of a screening program for COPD in primary care. The PADOC Project (Program for the Increase in the Diagnosis of COPD in Primary Care)</article-title><source>Arch. Bronconeumol.</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>500</fpage><lpage>505</lpage><year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11116545</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ekici</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekici</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurtipek</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Akin</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arslan</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kara</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Apaydin</surname><given-names>Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Demir</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obstructive airway diseases in women exposed to biomass smoke</article-title><source>Environ. Res.</source><volume>99</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16053933</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arora</surname><given-names>N.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rochester</surname><given-names>D.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Respiratory muscle strength and maximal voluntary ventilation in undernourished patients</article-title><source>Am. Rev. Respir. Dis.</source><volume>126</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><year>1982</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7091909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Engelen</surname><given-names>M.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schols</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Does</surname><given-names>J.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wouters</surname><given-names>E.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Skeletal muscle weakness is associated with wasting of extremity fat-free mass but not with airflow obstruction in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease</article-title><source>Am. J. Clin. Nutr.</source><volume>71</volume><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>738</lpage><year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10702166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wouters</surname><given-names>E.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nutrition and metabolism in COPD</article-title><source>Chest</source><volume>117</volume><fpage>274s</fpage><lpage>280s</lpage><year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10843949</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;1</label><caption><p>The effect of airway obstruction on nutritional parameters</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Parameters</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">COPD group (<italic>n</italic> = 450)</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Non-COPD group (<italic>n</italic> = 133)</th><th align="center" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>p</italic> level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">61.9 &#x000b1; 0.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60.9 &#x000b1; 0.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.28</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FVC (%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">69.3 &#x000b1; 1.0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">88.7 &#x000b1; 1.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FEV1 (%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">48.9 &#x000b1; 0.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">96.0 &#x000b1; 1.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FEV1/FVC (%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">55.3 &#x000b1; 0.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">78.7 &#x000b1; 0.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MMEF (%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21.9 &#x000b1; 0.5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">89.3 &#x000b1; 2.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PEF (%)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">39.2 &#x000b1; 0.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">85.3 &#x000b1; 1.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">BMI (kg.m<sup>&#x02212;2</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">26.1 &#x000b1; 0.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.5 &#x000b1; 0.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Haemoglobin (g.dL<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.8 &#x000b1; 0.1</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15.0 &#x000b1; 0.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.29</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Serum albumin (g.L<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.7 &#x000b1; 0.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">38.2 &#x000b1; 0.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.46</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Blood urea nitrogen (mg/dl)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21.9 &#x000b1; 0.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16.9 &#x000b1; 0.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Serum creatinine (mg/dl)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.33 &#x000b1; 0.03</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.00 &#x000b1; 0.03</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c;0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Serum creatine kinase (U/L)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">77.2 &#x000b1; 4.0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">96.4 &#x000b1; 9.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.06</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Serum cholesterol (mg/dl)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">174.5 &#x000b1; 7.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">179.9 &#x000b1; 6.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.59</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Serum triglycerides (mg/dl)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">136.7 &#x000b1; 12.1</td><td align="center" rowspan